  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "95mcy1sH57mJPNDYOqNIAbSGmsI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:07.943Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "M&I/Partners is vendor-neutral by design and has no build capability, so the only route through it is influence. What makes it more than a generic advisory entry is that it publishes the hospital IT benchmark, and the record cites healthcare IT spend at 6.0% of revenue.\n\nA published benchmark is a specific kind of leverage. It sets the figure hospital boards use to judge whether their own IT spend is reasonable, which means it shapes what counts as a normal investment before any vendor is in the room. Being read by the party that publishes that number is worth more than a referral from a firm holding no such instrument.\n\nBecause it cannot deliver anything, it does not compete for the application layer and it does not belong in the design-partner pool. It sits at priority 4 as an influence route.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**4 \u00b7 needs OSS screen**\n- M&I/Partners (NL)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> No build capability. Influence route: publishes the hospital IT benchmark (6.0% of revenue).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:30:07.943141Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:07.943146Z"
    }
  },
